WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.460
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:10.490
OpenAI's Gym was a selection of gaming environments
for reinforcement learning algorithms.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:15.769
This is a class of techniques that are able
to learn and perform an optimal chain of actions

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:17.180
in an environment.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:22.440
This environment could be playing video games,
navigating a drone around, or teaching digital

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.210
creatures to walk.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:30.180
In this system, people could create new reinforcement
learning programs and decide whose AI is the

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.180
best.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.289
Gym was a ton of fun, ... but have a look
this one!

00:00:34.289 --> 00:00:35.850
How is this different from Gym?

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.879
This new software platform, Universe works
not only for reinforcement learning algorithms,

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:43.850
but for arbitrary programs.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.890
Like a freestyle wrestling competition for
AI researchers!

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:55.190
The list of games include GTA V, Mirror's
Edge, Starcraft 2, Civilization 5, Minecraft,

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.789
Portal and a lot more this time around.

00:00:57.789 --> 00:00:59.159
Super exciting!

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:03.239
You can download this framework right now
and proceed testing.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:08.829
One can also perform different browser tasks,
such as booking a plane ticket and other endeavors

00:01:08.829 --> 00:01:12.600
that require navigating around in a web browser
interface.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.450
Given the current software architecture for
Universe, practically any task where automation

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.110
makes sense can be included in the future.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:25.520
And, we don't need to make any intrusive changes
to the game itself, in fact, we don't even

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.829
have to have access to the source code.

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:32.981
This is huge, especially given that many of
these games are proprietary software, so to

00:01:32.981 --> 00:01:38.049
make this happen, individual deals had taken
place between the game development companies

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:39.320
and OpenAI.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.720
When the company was founded by Elon Musk
and Sam Altman, they have picked up so many

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:47.110
of the most talented AI researchers around
the globe.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.479
And I am so happy to see that it really, really
shows.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:54.670
There is an excellent blog post describing
the details of the system, make sure to have

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:55.670
a look!

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.860
Also, I reckon that our comments section is
the absolute best I've seen on YouTube.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:06.189
Feel free to participate or start a discussion,
there are always plenty of amazing ideas in

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:07.299
the comments section.

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:11.079
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

